    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for high-ceiling production today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our premier efficiency score of 81.88. His massive matchup against Civale is boosted by a favorable park factor, wind assistance, and a prime leadoff spot, making him the centerpiece of our offensive strategy. Close behind in projected output is **Kyle Tucker** (75.90) and **Jackson Merrill** (74.04). Despite the intimidating presence of Spencer Strider on the mound, **Kyle Tucker** thrives on high-tier SP matchups, while **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a high-efficiency leadoff position against Dustin May. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.10) also secures a strong start, capitalizing on the weakest opposing starter on the board (Kochanowicz, 5.14 xERA), which offsets his slight platoon disadvantage.\n\nOur decision-making process for the utility spots heavily favored situational leverage over pure base power. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (67.75) and **Andy Pages** (67.55) both offer high-floor utility, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically benefiting from a strong dynamic platoon edge against Junk. On the fringes, **Miguel Vargas** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; his 54.01 score fell just short of the efficiency threshold required to displace **Josh Lowe** (57.15) or **Coby Mayo** (57.41). While **Miguel Vargas** remains a high-upside asset, the optimizer prioritized the volume of plate appearances and the superior park factors favoring **Coby Mayo** in his matchup against Civale.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the lineup uncertainty for **Drake Baldwin**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jackson Merrill**, as all rely on assumed batting order placements. While these players carry high projection scores, any deviation from their projected spots could lower their expected run and RBI contribution. We are comfortable with **Josh Lowe** in the nine-hole for now, though his efficiency is tethered to his lower lineup placement despite a solid matchup against Yesavage. Keep a close watch on pre-game weather reports for wind shifts; while the current wind-out projections are providing a healthy lift to **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Sam Antonacci**, any late-breaking meteorological changes could tighten the margins for our middle-of-the-pack starters.",
